Revision history for manage-skills

{{$NEXT}}

0.11.2    2026-10-06 15:58:12Z
  - Works from a Windows checkout under Git Bash: `bin/manage-skills` is a
    script instead of a symlink.

0.11.1    2026-08-25 14:54:22Z
  - Every install route is registered and reported correctly.

0.11.0    2026-08-25 04:07:08Z
  - Reports files a project has that no source does.

0.10.0    2026-08-22 04:33:43Z
  - The numbered menu takes several numbers at once.

0.9.0     2026-08-22 04:20:27Z
  - A bare owner name resolves to that owner's skills repo.
  - Every file in a skill directory is linked, not just `SKILL.md`.

0.8.1     2026-08-19 03:55:37Z
  - Symlinked skill directories are skipped during discovery.
  - Grouped skills are discovered in local sources too.

0.8.0     2026-08-18 05:08:38Z
  - Diverged copies are kept unless `sync` is forced.

0.7.1     2026-08-18 03:58:29Z
  - The Codex manifest is bumped with every release.

0.7.0     2026-08-18 03:56:22Z
  - manage-skills ships to Codex as well.

0.6.0     2026-08-18 03:18:57Z
  - Skills that a source groups into subdirectories are found.

0.5.0     2026-08-18 01:16:33Z
  - Serves Codex too: the same skills directory, a second manifest.
  - `package` makes a skill set installable by people who do not use
    manage-skills.

0.4.0     2026-08-18 01:15:22Z
  - Remote sources, so skills can be shared without Claude Code.

0.3.0     2026-08-18 01:13:27Z
  - Ships as a Claude Code plugin and marketplace.
  - Listings are laid out in columns; `locations` and `self` are new.
  - `shorten()` no longer emits a literal backslash on bash 3.2.
  - Four failures the test suite was hiding are corrected.

0.2.0     2026-05-07 15:48:48Z
  - First tagged release: hardlink-based skill sharing across projects, with
    CI, the release workflow and smoke tests.
  - Runs on bash 3.2: no associative arrays.
